{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q6695106","formula":"C₁₄H₁₈FNO₂","hill":"C14H18FNO2","elements":["H","C","N","O","F"],"composition":{"C":14.0,"F":1.0,"H":18.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"Lubazodone"},"descriptions":{"en":"Lubazodone (developmental code names YM-992, YM-35995) is an experimental antidepressant which was under development by Yamanouchi for the treatment for major depressive disorder in the late 1990s and early 2000s but was never marketed. It acts as a serotonin reuptake inhibitor (Ki for SERTTooltip serotonin transporter = 21 nM) and 5-HT2A receptor antagonist (Ki = 86 nM), and hence has the profile of a serotonin antagonist and reuptake inhibitor (SARI). The drug has good selectivity against a range of other monoamine receptors, with its next highest affinities being for the α1-adrenergic receptor (Ki = 200 nM) and the 5-HT2C receptor (Ki = 680 nM)."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":157919,"mass":251.3,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1CC2=C(C=CC(=C2C1)F)OC[C@@H]3CNCCO3","inchikey":"HTODIQZHVCHVGM-JTQLQIEISA-N","iupac":"(2S)-2-[(7-fluoro-2,3-dihydro-1H-inden-4-yl)oxymethyl]morpholine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"157919","atoms":36,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-4.793,"y":-0.865,"z":0.528,"el":"F"},{"x":3.357,"y":-0.516,"z":-1.038,"el":"O"},{"x":0.607,"y":-0.514,"z":-0.586,"el":"O"},{"x":4.098,"y":0.75,"z":1.399,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.075,"y":1.971,"z":-0.309,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.506,"y":0.541,"z":-0.214,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.425,"y":2.676,"z":-0.512,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.484,"y":1.812,"z":0.188,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.874,"y":0.451,"z":0.069,"el":"C"},{"x":2.826,"y":-0.983,"z":0.208,"el":"C"},{"x":2.765,"y":0.173,"z":1.21,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.724,"y":-0.595,"z":-0.327,"el":"C"},{"x":1.438,"y":-1.549,"z":-0.061,"el":"C"},{"x":4.649,"y":1.181,"z":0.113,"el":"C"},{"x":4.672